  :project agentic-systems

  |title Keep pushing until you're well past it, or until you can say exactly why it can't be done

  |quote
    what I remember saying was "keep pushing until you're well past it or until you can come back and say exactly why it can't be done and what insight *that* result means for the project..."

  |occasion
    Checking how a spike had actually been briefed — he is reconstructing his own
    earlier instruction because the agent's version of it had lost the second half.

  |about
    The spike disposition with both terminating conditions, and they are not success and
    failure. They are *past the claim* and *an exact account of why not, plus what that
    account means* — the second being a result in its own right rather than a write-off.
    What went missing in transmission was precisely the clause that makes a no-go
    valuable.

  |before-acting
    - You are about to report that an approach did not work.
    - You are deciding when a spike is finished.
    - You are briefing someone else on an exploratory task.
    - You have a negative result and are treating it as an absence of a result.

  |see
    - #exm-always-do-a-strengthening-pass

